Subject: Gate SELinux status on active hiding, not saved intent

Target: common android15-6.6 after the pinned SUSFS and sehide1 patches.
A late enable may return EAGAIN after the backup policy was dropped.
KernelSU deliberately retains enabled=1 for the next boot while running=0.
Context/access queries use running, but status open used enabled and could
select the snapshot alone. Use the same effective-state gate for status.
Preserve the existing save-and-reboot contract and status contents.
This does not address detectors operating with hiding successfully active.

diff --git a/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c b/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c
--- a/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c
+++ b/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c
@@ -249,7 +249,8 @@
 	void *data;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (likely(current_uid().val >= 10000 && ksu_selinux_hide_enabled)) {
+	/* A saved enable request can still be waiting for a reboot. */
+	if (likely(current_uid().val >= 10000 && ksu_selinux_hide_running)) {
 		mutex_lock(&selinux_state.status_lock);
 		data = fake_status;
 		mutex_unlock(&selinux_state.status_lock);
